WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
*slurp*

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.680
mmm, that's some good sh*t

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.360
Hey, everyone! What's happening? You might be thinking,

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.080
"Wow! Mayuko, you're gonna make a whole YouTube channel out of this thing?"

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.200
Why? Yes, I am.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.420
You may have heard from me already that I went to Vidcon a couple weeks ago with some really good friends

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.740
And I left feeling so motivated and inspired and empowered.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.280
I met creators that I admired for a long time,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.320
got to go to panels and parties and

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.680
Overall just had such a great time at Vidcon!

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:37.160
And I think the main thing that I took away from Vidcon was that there's room on the internet for everyone,

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.640
including you and me. So that's partly one of the reasons why I decided to make a YouTube channel

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:48.080
The other thing is that I'm really empowered by people like Simone Giertz and Physics Girl and the impact that they have on young women

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.580
to pursue careers and an interest in technology in science

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:57.180
And if I could have that kind of impact on just one person, I think that would be SO cool.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:00.629
I've been working in tech for about three years now at two different companies

00:01:00.629 --> 00:01:03.838
And so I thought I'd share with you today six reasons

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:09.160
why I love being a software engineer. Number one: innovation is everywhere, and it's really cool.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:13.000
I live in Silicon Valley, so I literally live in the middle of the Tech hub.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.680
Living in the middle of Silicon Valley and being able to experience how quickly the innovation is

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:23.880
going and how quickly new things are coming out is really inspiring.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.340
Number two: I think one of the best things about software engineering

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:33.260
is that you can apply your skills to anything. For instance you can make health apps that monitor the blood sugar levels of patients

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:38.760
Or you can make educational apps that help teachers organize their coursework more easily.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.580
Or you can even make code that gets sent up into space!

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.380
*pop*

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.520
That is so cool

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:51.360
So this actually has a lot to do with why I went into software engineering as a career and studied computer science to begin with.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:56.500
I didn't really know what exactly what industry that I wanted to go into,

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:02.060
but I did want to have the freedom to be able to choose throughout my whole career and not limit myself.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.260
Number three is: collaboration

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:09.500
Working in tech actually means that you get to work with so many different kinds of people. On the daily I get to work with:

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:13.860
A product manager who decides what we work on and why it's important

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.460
A designers who decides

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.780
"How is it going to look and how is it going to feel when a user is working on it?"

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.160
of course other software engineers

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:24.160
who I'm working with and solving these problems with as I'm building.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.120
And also I get the opportunity to work with

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.500
data scientists, marketing people, support people

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:34.260
It's just so cool to be able to work with so many different kinds of people who think in such different ways

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:39.180
And to be able to create a product together that you can deliver out into the world.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.020
Number four is: problem-solving

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:45.940
So coding is really just problem-solving. So you have a problem in front of you

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:52.780
Which is usually "how do I build this thing?" and then you make the code and you problem-solve through that to build that thing.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:56.580
And one of my favorite things about software engineering is that you can spend a lot of time

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.040
researching the problem

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.450
trying out different things

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:04.480
talking about it with other people and the next thing you know you have a solution to the problem that you're working on

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:10.160
and sometimes it takes thirty minutes, sometimes it takes three days, sometimes it takes a whole month

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.880
And thats not to say that creativity isn't involved in the job

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:18.880
because it so is! because problem-solving is not just a matter of doing formulas and equations and stuff

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.520
but it's really thinking creatively about how to solve the problem that's right in front of you.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.820
Number five is that you're always learning!

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:28.300
so this actually refers back to number one which is about innovation

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:34.720
Because innovation is literally just about kind of the invention of new stuff all the time, it kind of goes along with

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.799
Your job as a software engineer

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.440
because there's always new stuff coming out. Whether it be a new programming language or a new framework

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:49.120
Or a new architecture and so having this skill of being able to adapt to new things is really important

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.140
And that's something that companies often look for.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.000
But in my opinion,

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.480
It's always fun to be in an area where new things are coming out all the time

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:01.180
Because then there's always something new to learn and grab and add to your skill set.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:01.840
Okay

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.649
So my last and final reason why I love being a software engineer

00:04:05.649 --> 00:04:07.400
is probably my most favorite.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.460
Number six is impact.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.180
So because of the nature of code and

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.520
electronics and computers and stuff your code can be on an

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:17.209
*???*

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:20.000
infinite number of devices all around the world and

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:27.600
and usually if you're building an app or something you're at least going to reach thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, sometimes millions of people

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.849
And it's really cool to know that what you're building is

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.120
affecting so many people out there

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.420
And if you have the chance to meet the people who you're writing these apps for

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:42.800
Then it's an amazing feeling when someone tells you: hey, your app has made my life so much easier

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:48.460
And the other side is that you don't just have an impact on the people that you're writing code for

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:54.460
But you also have an impact on your peers around you. It's really awesome to help each other grow

00:04:54.900 --> 00:05:00.620
As you build something really cool. So that concludes the six reasons why I love working as a software engineer

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.020
It's a really rewarding career

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:07.070
And I've been loving it so far and if you have any other career related

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:10.780
questions for me about being a software engineer or being a woman in tech

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:14.900
Or anything at all! Let me know. I would love to answer them

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:19.560
I hope this video is helpful, and I'll see you next time. Have a good day!!!

